WEBVTT

00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:13,900
If I genetically do not convert beta-carotene into vitamin A,

00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:16,700
is there any sense in juicing carrots?

00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:26,940
So nobody genetically does not convert beta-carotene into vitamin A.

00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:33,100
If you have those G defects, the MCO or whatever they are,

00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:39,340
then you have a more difficult time in that conversion.

00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:45,420
So people that have a lot of defects in that gene family,

00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:53,980
it would make sense for them to consume more vitamin A even as beta-carotene

00:00:54,860 --> 00:01:04,300
because you need healthier dose of that in order to have an adequate amount of vitamin A reserves

00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:11,180
for use in your body. So yes, to answer this question, if I have that genetic defect,

00:01:11,660 --> 00:01:18,140
where I don't convert or have the possibility of not converting beta-carotene into vitamin A as well

00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:22,620
if I didn't have that defect, is there a sense that you see carrots?

00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:25,660
Absolutely, there is probably a greater need to do so.

00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:33,100
Not that. You can't get beta-carotene and vitamin A from other sources, so I'm not saying that this

00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:45,180
is a reason to do carrot. But if you want to do carrot juicing and you want to gain the nutrients

00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:50,540
from the carrots and you have a beta-carotene, it's just one nutrient that you gain from

00:01:50,540 --> 00:02:01,020
juicing carrots. So because you have that gene, it would not hinder you from making that decision to

00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:09,340
introduce them, so I would say yes, go ahead with that.

